WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:02.660
- I wanna discuss a serious
topic with you as well.

00:00:02.660 --> 00:00:06.770
So we're seeing protests
against anti-Asian violence.

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:09.190
And I just wanna know your thoughts on it.

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:12.260
- It's actually, what's been
happening has been incredible.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:14.290
I think a lot of, a lot of
people have been reaching

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:17.580
out to me and wondering how
they can help, what they can do.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:20.660
And I love to post tangible
things that people can do

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:22.661
'cause there's all sorts
of performative activism.

00:00:22.661 --> 00:00:23.494
- Mmhmm.

00:00:23.494 --> 00:00:27.821
- I think we just came out
of a long line of politicians

00:00:27.821 --> 00:00:31.100
that put a target on Asian people's backs

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:33.110
by calling it the China virus.

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:36.670
And so people are seeing Asian
people out on the street.

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:39.720
I automatically think of like
when my mom's without me,

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:40.560
how do people look at her?

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:42.320
How do people treat her?

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:45.240
A lot of mothers and
fathers are being targeted

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:48.553
around the country and it is so,

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:52.950
it's so obvious to me what the motive is.

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:55.150
It's not, it doesn't seem to
be obvious to the politicians

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:56.240
out there that are saying like,

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:58.160
we're not quite sure of the motive.

00:00:58.160 --> 00:00:59.530
But I think we know what it is

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:03.320
and if people can just
reach out in any way

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:06.453
to support the Asian-American community.

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:11.200
AAPI in general, there's Stop AAPI Hate

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:13.410
which is a wonderful
organization to donate to.

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:16.190
And an organization
called 18 Million Rising

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:17.030
is really incredible.

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:18.950
But also support, it's little things

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:21.360
like supporting Asian owned
businesses around you,

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:23.010
supporting your local China Town.

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:25.100
I mean these things are disappearing

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:27.520
quicker than we know it, and
soon they're gonna be gone,

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:30.267
and it's heartbreaking to me, so.

